      // 0x1053d8c (READ whole): a slot at 0 (bare) or 4 (broken) -> 0; at 1 on variant 4 -> it breaks whatever the damage; at 2 / 3 the
      // damage dmg x [0xba9f0(e, 2)+0xc] (at least 1 when dmg > 0) comes off part 1's durability P+0x3cc and breaks at <= 0. The viewer:
      // the slot is the trunk row SHOWN (input.trunkSnow083, motion-states.js trunkSnow083); dmg 999 ((7, 0x10 / 0x11 / 0x35 / 0x36),
      // tune ints 0x22 / 0x23) is taken to break 2 / 3 -- the durability is not an input (INFERRED); dmg 0 ((7, 0x42), int 0x24)
      // breaks only a slot at 1. Part 1's break level is 0 unless the trunk was broken, which the shown slot 4 already says (a regrown
